        <div class="pm-faq">
          <div class="pm-faq-item"><h3>1. What performance-marketing packages do you offer for brands in Mumbai?</h3><div>4 transparent retainer tiers: <strong>Starter Rs 25,000/mo</strong> (solo founders, 1 paid channel), <strong>Growth Rs 35,000/mo</strong> (2-3 SKU scaling, full paid stack), <strong>Performance Pro Rs 45,000/mo</strong> (multi-channel + attribution), <strong>Enterprise Rs 55,000/mo</strong> (multi-market + MMM). Plus 6 performance-linked models: commission (10-20% ad spend), revenue-share (5-15% GMV), per-lead (Rs 500-3K), per-order (Rs 200-2K), ROAS-guaranteed, hybrid. Ad spend separate + zero markup.</div></div>
          <div class="pm-faq-item"><h3>2. How much ad spend do we need for brands in Mumbai?</h3><div>Realistic monthly ad-spend bands: Starter package Rs 30K-1L, Growth Rs 1-5L, Performance Pro Rs 5-15L, Enterprise Rs 15L-1Cr+. Ad spend is SEPARATE from retainer + pass-through — you see exactly what Meta/Google bill. ITD manages Rs 8Cr+ annual ad spend across 20+ D2C + B2B + B2C brands.</div></div>
          <div class="pm-faq-item"><h3>3. What is the difference between retainer + commission-based + revenue-share models?</h3><div>Retainer = fixed monthly fee (Rs 25K-55K), predictable cost. Commission = 10-20% of ad spend, scales with your investment (better for Rs 3L+ ad spend). Revenue-share = 5-15% of ad-attributed revenue (aligns agency to your top-line — best for Rs 15L+ monthly GMV). Per-lead + per-order = pay only for outcomes (Rs 500-3K/lead, Rs 200-2K/order). Choose based on cash-flow preference + ad-spend size + risk appetite.</div></div>
          <div class="pm-faq-item"><h3>4. Do you have real client case studies for brands in Mumbai?</h3><div>Yes — ITD manages performance marketing for 20+ active brands across D2C fashion, jewelry, beauty, F&B, home, wellness, plus B2B SaaS + real estate + healthcare + clinic verticals. Live client dashboards + case study PDFs shared under NDA on discovery call. Specific brand names anonymized publicly to protect client confidentiality.</div></div>
